@startuml BUG-115_as_is
title BUG-115 — AS-IS: the QtWidgets↔QML bridge is a convention repeated per host, not an abstraction

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Engine (unused by the app)" #EEEEEE {
  class "create_quick_widget()" as factory <<function>> {
    ensure_qml_style()
    register_theme()
    addImportPath(Sagittarius.UI)
    addImageProvider(icons)
    -- clear colour: Qt default (opaque white) --
  }
}

package "App — 10 hand-rolled hosts (+7 preview.py)" {
  abstract class QQuickWidget <<Qt>>

  class QmlOverlay {
    _quick = QQuickWidget()
    setClearColor(transparent)
    setContextProperty(Theme)
    setSource / raise
    root_object
  }
  class SymbolPickerModal
  class MetricsDetailModal
  class DatabaseStatusPanel
  class PositionsPanel
  class OpenOrdersPanel

  class ChartToolbar
  class ProgressBannerWidget
  class StatusPillWidget
  class StatCardRowWidget

  QmlOverlay o-- QQuickWidget : composes (6 hosts)
  SymbolPickerModal o-- QQuickWidget
  MetricsDetailModal o-- QQuickWidget
  DatabaseStatusPanel o-- QQuickWidget
  PositionsPanel o-- QQuickWidget
  OpenOrdersPanel o-- QQuickWidget

  QQuickWidget <|-- ChartToolbar : subclasses (4 hosts)
  QQuickWidget <|-- ProgressBannerWidget
  QQuickWidget <|-- StatusPillWidget
  QQuickWidget <|-- StatCardRowWidget

  class "qml/style.py\nensure_qml_style()" as appstyle <<copy of engine's>>
}

note right of QmlOverlay
  Every host repeats the same 12 lines:
  style pin, Theme, context lifetime, load+raise,
  resize mode, **setClearColor(transparent)** +
  comment "so the parent SURFACE shows through".
  The assumption is only true on the software
  paint path (offscreen / widget.grab()); on the
  texture path Qt punches a hole in the backing
  store and clears to black → BUG-102 / BUG-115.
  No guard stops an 11th copy.
end note

note bottom of factory
  Exists exactly to prevent "hand-rolling a partial
  copy" (its own docstring) — bypassed 17 times
  after EPIC-006F removed configure_app_qml()
  from bootstrap and EPIC-015 brought QML back.
end note
@enduml
